          "timestamp": "2026-11-27T23:18:49Z",
          "message": "Merge 26cfd3805b0c22cb7042e0abedba51dbd0f49a41 into dfd45a29e6c86fc420ccaa588ea8bd9796bf270c\n"
        },
        {
          "sha": "26cfd3805b0c22cb7042e0abedba51dbd0f49a41",
          "author_name": "Brandon Fryslie",
          "author_email": "530235+brandon-fryslie@users.noreply.github.com",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-27T16:18:34-07:00",
          "message": "fix(stored-state): a file's standing is kept by its cause, and told once per change\n\nA failed write's message names a staged file unique to the attempt, so a\nstanding compared by text restated the bar on every refusal. The holder\nkeeps the standing by the error's code and tells the daemon the error whole.\nThe history storage shares the one Landings the other storages tell through,\nthe write-failure rows have their own map, a standing's set and clear are\nlogged, and close and take keep their error boundaries.\n"
        },
        {
          "sha": "981a59cda6ec187cf4d2c54eec94b97c2d2a268f",
          "author_name": "Brandon Fryslie",
          "author_email": "530235+brandon-fryslie@users.noreply.github.com",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-27T15:58:02-07:00",
          "message": "fix(stored-state): a per-session file whose write fails stands behind on every bar\n\nA write behind has no caller to throw into, so its failure reached only the\ndaemon log. Each per-session storage now tells its holder what every write came\nto, and the daemon keeps one standing warning per file until a write lands.\nThe settings history writes at once but is told the same way, so its failure is\none row in the same words instead of a second act failure that left the bar\nwhen its hold ended.\n"
        }
      ]
    },
